      "message": "(Continued from PS7)\n\nI believe std::function is copyable. So the lambda could take these parameters by value, instead of by reference.\n\nIf that\u0027s not possible, then I\u0027d argue that we should do two things:\n- Pass these parameters as pointers, rather than references. Seeing the \u0027\u0026\u0027 at the call-site would make us more conscious of the need to worry about the object lifetime.\n- Update the startGscan() documentation, to make explicit that the result callbacks must be valid until stopGscan() has been called. (I can sort of infer that requirement from the current documentation. But I\u0027d rather be explicit about lifetime requirements.)\n\nNote that, at present, there\u0027s nothing to warn the caller that they shouldn\u0027t use lambdas for their callbacks.",
