      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if we should do a little more validation, before returning the results. Specifically... should we ensure that ie_length of each |wifi_scan_result| is 0?\n\nConsider the following situation:\n- driver\u0027s wifi_get_cached_gscan_results() naively copies IE data into wifi_scan_results. (this is buggy, because the IE info would overlap the next scan result. but i\u0027d like to be robust to bugs where it\u0027s reasonably possible.)\n- upper layers use the same code to wifi_scan_result, regardless of whether the result is coming from a gscan event, or from a full result\n- in this case, upper layers will provide garbage IEs, and also overrun the buffer\n\nWe could avoid this by checking that all the |ie_length| fields are zero here. If a non-zero value is found, either a) zero it, and log a message, or b) abort. (I\u0027d lean towards zero-and-log, since I think that\u0027ll fixup the data in any common buggy case. But maybe I\u0027m not being imaginative enough, about likely bugs.)\n\n(Sorry I didn\u0027t mention this in the previous revision!)",
